  "security_implications": "msg_mask_permuted is generated from static_mask and RndCnstMsgPerm for message masking. If the mask values or the permutation are not cryptographically independent from secret data, an attacker could extract side-channel information. The static nature of the mask (instead of LFSR) may reduce resistance to differential power/EM analysis. Additionally, a mismatch in MsgWidth could lead to incomplete masking of full-width secret data.",
